{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Along about [D]round-up time In [G]Texas way out [D]West[D]
[D]I lost a [D]friend and a pal, boys I [E]laid him down to [A]rest
[D]I weeped and moaned [D]over his grave and to [G]me boys it was [D]sad
[G]'Cause I knew down [D]beneath that mound lay the [A]best pal I ever [D]had[D]
{end_of_verse}

